<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexandre Pétion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1770">1770</a>–<a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexandre Pétion was a Haitian revolutionary leader and the first president of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> in the south and west, from 1807 to 1818. Unlike <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-christophe">Henri Christophe</a>'s northern kingdom, his republic distributed state lands to soldiers and peasants. He gave refuge and aid to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> in 1815 and 1816.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexandre-petion.jpg" alt="Alexandre Pétion" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: lithographer unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexandre_Sab%C3%A9s_P%C3%A9tion_Portrait_circa_1807-1818_JCB_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
